Z||000005||hutch84fierose||09-17-2001||06:14 AM||||That car is sweet color sweet too.  About the interior how do you get brushed aluminum??????????<BR>I am thinking about painting my car i heard there is some specail kinda paint for fieros? is this true a painter told me this its gonna cost a lot of money to paint it.  He said something about a FLEX AGENT so the plastic panels can flex.  He also said I have to do the car the same colour or it will be alot more money to change colours what has to be done to the car???????<BR>thanksa for the help........i don't want to spend 1000's to paint a car really||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||09-17-2001||06:24 AM||||Yes the paint does need a flex agent with the duraflex panels of a Fiero.<BR>The Fiero though is probably one of the easier cars to change colours on though due to most panel undersides and inside doors etc is black. It really is just the outer skins that need painting. <BR>A good paintjob does cost a lot though. I am tossing up whether to buy a new compressor and stuff to do it myself (used to work as a spraypainter way back when) or to outlay $3000 and have my local custom paint guys do it. ||||reg||1
